WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.710
- If I wake up and everybody
in my family is alive,

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:05.280
I'm so fucking fired
up, I don't watch shit,

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.683
I don't listen to shit, I'm so grateful.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.130
Gratitude, it's just gratitude,

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:15.540
like one life, one at bat, one time.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.140
I'm fascinated by people thinking

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:20.591
that gratitude is the
same word as complacent.

00:00:20.591 --> 00:00:22.163
I think people mix words a lot.

00:00:23.598 --> 00:00:26.181
(upbeat music)

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:28.800
The biggest fear I have

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.880
is for the people that are
actually having success,

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.920
because complacency kicks in

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:35.723
and you just get into pattern recognition.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.620
When it's about getting a watch,

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.920
or buying a new home,

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.300
or getting a new pair of
Yeezy's, you're finished.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.430
And so I see a lot of people

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:50.620
looking for quick highs.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.730
I want to get that girl,
I want to get that guy,

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:53.810
I want to get that plane,

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:58.010
I want to get that car, that
is just not sustainable.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:01.310
Everybody is looking for
so much outside validation

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:02.350
that they're impatient,

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.900
they want to show everybody
they're successful,

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.270
thus they're rushing into things.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:08.220
You have 23 year olds who think

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.730
that they don't have
their life figured out

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:11.983
yet they're living for another 80 years.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.940
What progression?

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:19.350
Title, an extra zero in your bank account,

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.890
buying dumb shit.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:22.890
Happiness is the fucking progression.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.150
Most people hear the word patience

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:28.660
and have it confused with
complacency, laziness,

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.700
lack of ambition.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.730
It's not true, I actually think patience

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:34.040
has been foundational in my success.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:36.250
I decided to build my
dad's business for him

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.180
for the first 12 years of my career,

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.570
that required huge patience

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.420
from somebody who thought they were great.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.870
I didn't even start quote
unquote until I was 34.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.570
Patience is huge, it's huge,

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:47.610
and people don't wanna do it

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.360
because they want instant gratification,

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.150
and more importantly,
instant outside validation.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.710
I mean I am so competitive and hungry

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.490
it's probably inappropriate.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:01.553
At the same token, I genuinely am content.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:06.050
Being content and
grateful for what you have

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:08.760
and not envious for what you don't have

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.930
while still being ambitious

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.430
is a different way to think
about being satisfied.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:15.510
You know there's a reason why

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:16.900
there's a word called gratitude,

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.992
and there's a reason why there's
a word called complacency.

00:02:19.992 --> 00:02:21.430
And I use gratitude and patience a lot

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:23.570
and I think people think
it's an excuse for laziness

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.110
or not going to get it,

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:27.550
and I laugh at that because
there's a whole nother world

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.990
that thinks that I'm saying go too hard

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:34.200
and all this does on both
sides of the conversation

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.850
is excuses people for
finding in my message

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:40.410
what they're looking
for which is cynicism.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.980
Their cynical point of view.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:44.510
I'm talking about being
grateful and patient

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.550
while having tremendous work ethic

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.560
and tenacity and ambition.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:53.860
Gratitude is my fuel, I'm
grateful, like I'm alive.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:55.600
Yeah I keep things very basic,

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.480
as long as my family's healthy,

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.800
it's hard for me to get down.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.350
So I'm just grateful, you know.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:04.830
When you're like I can
not believe I'm alive,

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.680
thank you so much,

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.830
and oh my god I can't wait to wake up

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.510
and fight and grind and try to win,

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:13.120
I love the game.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.403
You're unstoppable.

